The box plot illustrates that Nano-11, a dendrimer-like alpha-D-glucan nanoparticle, serves as an effective vaccine adjuvant, inducing significantly higher anti-rPA IgG titers in mice compared to rPA antigen alone. At higher doses (200 µg and 50 µg), Nano-11 demonstrates comparable adjuvanticity to aluminum hydroxide (AH). Notably, at a low dose of 12.5 µg, Nano-11 still elicits a strong antibody response, whereas AH at the same low dose fails to significantly enhance titers, indicating Nano-11's superior immunopotentiating effect at lower concentrations.